1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,780
Jump into the sea off Orkney

2
00:00:01,780 --> 00:00:02,410
in winter,

3
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:04,030
and you have about one minute.

4
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:06,610
Last time you met the selkie.

5
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:08,570
Could one work?

6
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:11,010
The water is seven degrees.

7
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:13,460
A person gasps in the first

8
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:13,910
minute,

9
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:15,290
is helpless within ten,

10
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:17,510
and gets hypothermia within an hour.

11
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:19,340
So you wear fat,

12
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:20,350
like a harbour seal.

13
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:22,910
Blubber keeps the body warm.

14
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:24,620
But selkies hunt,

15
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:25,860
so you must hold your breath.

16
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:28,460
Grey seals feed at seventy meters

17
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:29,230
or more.

18
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:30,940
So slow your heart,

19
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:32,010
like a grey seal.

20
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:34,140
On long dives it drops to

21
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:35,170
four beats a minute.

22
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:37,700
But a female grey seal weighs

23
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:39,730
a hundred and fifty five kilos.

24
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:41,980
Where does it all go when

25
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:43,330
she turns into a person?

26
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:45,750
No fix for that one.

27
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:47,510
But here's the twist.

28
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:50,040
Real seals do shed.

29
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:53,200
Harbour seals spend long stretches ashore

30
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:54,090
when they molt.

31
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:56,660
So maybe the legend began with

32
00:00:56,660 --> 00:00:57,810
a seal on a rock,

33
00:00:58,020 --> 00:00:58,970
losing its coat.

